    fix(core-data, crypto): runtime validation + zeroization hardening (P1 A-group)
    
    Why:
    Codex cross-vendor review on `codex/track-a-desktop-foundation` flagged
    three runtime-validation gaps and one zeroization gap that allowed
    malformed or sensitive material to bypass guards documented in
    `docs/contracts/data-repository-v0.md` and the G2.4 keychain bridge.
    
    What:
    - A1: `assertRepoRecord()` now enforces the documented
      `^[a-z]+\.[a-z_]+$` regex via a module-level `ENTITY_TYPE_RE`,
      refining the E3005 message to name the offending value.
    - A2: `assertRepoRecord()` adds a runtime check rejecting any
      `clipboard.item` record whose `syncScope` is not `device-local`,
      closing the gap between the TS-level narrowing on
      `ClipboardEntryEntity` and rows fetched from SQLite.
    - A3: `migrateOrganizerLayoutToRepos()` performs positive validation in
      `toGridItemEntity()`: legacy items must have a non-empty `filepath`
      and a `file|folder|app` kind; everything else (including any url
      shape) is dropped and counted via a new
      `OrganizerLayoutMigrationResult.skipped` field.
    - A4: `insert_kek_from_bytes()` now zeroizes the caller buffer on the
      length-error early-return path AND wraps the stack-local
      `[u8; KEY_BYTES]` in `zeroize::Zeroizing` so the local copy is
      scrubbed when it drops, eliminating the leftover stack value.
    
    Scope:
    - packages/core-data/src/repo-utils.ts
    - packages/core-data/src/organizer-layout-migration.ts
    - packages/core-data/tests/entities.test.ts
    - packages/core-data/tests/organizer-layout-migration.test.ts
    - apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/crypto/keychain_handle.rs
    
    Risk:
    Low. Pure runtime-validation tightening + defence-in-depth zeroization.
    No public API or schema change; `OrganizerLayoutMigrationResult` only
    gains a new optional field consumers can ignore. The zeroize crate was
    already enabled behind the `crypto` feature.
    
    Docs:
    No doc churn required — the regex and `device-local` invariant are
    already documented in `docs/contracts/data-repository-v0.md`; this
    change brings the runtime in line with the contract.
    
    Tests:
    - `pnpm --filter @repo/core-data test` — 7 files / 69 tests pass
